<title>MALAYSIA: Hyundai, MISC in $102m ship deal.</title>
<headline>Hyundai, MISC in $102m ship deal.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-09-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hyundai Corp of South Korea has been awarded a $102 million contract to build two container ships for Malaysian International Shipping Corp (MISC), The Star newspaper reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>The agreement, signed on Friday, requires Hyundai to deliver two vessels of 2,700 twenty food equivalent (TEU) each to MISC by June 1998, The Star quoted MISC managing director Ariffin Elias as saying.</p>
<p>MISC currently owns 58 vessels and plans to increase its fleet size to 100 by the year 2000, the managing director said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur Newsroom (603) 201 4813</p>
